# Logging: Loguru only

Use [Loguru](https://github.com/Delgan/loguru) for all application logging. Do not add `import logging` / `logging.getLogger` in app code.

## Setup

- Configure once at process start via `pdfindex.logging_config.configure_logging()` (see `main.py`).
- Import the shared logger: `from loguru import logger`.

## Patterns

```python
# Messages use brace formatting (not %-style, prefer over f-strings for lazy eval)
logger.info('Processing PDF: {}', pdf_path)

# Structured context via bind()
logger.bind(pdf_path=pdf_path, page_count=n).info('Extracted PDF pages')

# Pretty JSON / multi-line payloads
logger.debug('Claude final_response:\n{}', parsed.model_dump_json(indent=2))

# Catch unexpected failures at entrypoints
@logger.catch(reraise=True)
def main(...):
  ...

# Descriptive exceptions (diagnose/backtrace enabled in configure_logging)
logger.exception('Validation error for Codex response')
```

## Do not

- Use stdlib `logging.basicConfig` / handlers in app modules.
- Log giant SDK object `repr`s; log the validated / pretty payload instead.
- Swallow exceptions without `logger.exception` (or `logger.opt(exception=True)`).
